Key Market Drivers
1. Rising Demand for Plant Based Protein
The Spirulina market recorded USD 160 million in 2025, reflecting a steady uptake among consumers seeking alternatives to animal protein. The alga’s 60–70 % protein concentration, combined with a complete amino acid profile, positions it as a premium ingredient in protein powders, fortified beverages and snack bars. Brands that embed spirulina into clean label formulations capture higher price premiums and benefit from repeat purchase cycles.
2. Regulatory Endorsements for Nutraceuticals
More than 18 national nutrition programmes list spirulina as a recommended supplement, while the WHO cites it as a viable solution for micronutrient deficiencies. Recent FDA clearances for spirulina infused functional foods have reduced time to market for innovators, encouraging faster product launches across retail channels.
